TI  - Educator Perspectives on a Collaborative Integration of ChatGPT to Foster EFL Learner Autonomy in the Development of Speaking and Writing Skills
AB  - This paper repor ts on a collaborative teacher innovation that integrated ChatGPT into English as a Foreign Language (EFL) courses at a Japanese junior college. Three instructors designed lesson sequences for three course strands, speaking, presentation, and writing in order to support students preparing for study abroad. Each strand included a series of three ChatGPTmediated lessons that emphasized prompt literacy, reflective learning, and ethical use of AI. Teacher reflections showed encouraging results: students were more engaged, motivated, and independent, and they developed a more critical and confident approach to AI. Challenges included differences in digital skills, occasional overreliance on AI, and technical limits of the free version of ChatGPT. Overall, the project demonstrates how cross-skill integration of ChatGPT can enhance student confidence, academic performance, and ethical awareness, while helping teachers adapt to evolving AI technologies.
