TY  - RPRT
TI  - Machine Economic Agency: Risk-First Longitudinal Evaluation of Financial LLM Agents
AB  - This preprint introduces machine economic agency: a framing for financial AI systems whose decisions are embedded in economic feedback loops. The work instantiates the idea through WisdomBench-Finance, a risk-first longitudinal evaluation protocol for financial LLM agents. Each decision is recorded as a causal tuple of visible evidence, pre-policy intent, risk-gate reasons, final action, execution metadata, audit trace, and later same-run market outcomes. On an audit-valid paper-market runtime spanning 64,244 decisions and 3,220 cycles across 20 assets, risk governance changes behavior materially: 30.27% of rows touch at least one risk gate and 10,971 non-neutral candidate actions are suppressed to neutral. Same-run realization joins show a horizon-dependent profile: the active cohort is negative at 1d but positive at 3d and 5d. These results are presented as audit and benchmark evidence, not as alpha dominance, live-money robustness, or investment advice.
