TY  - JOUR
TI  - Quantifying Uncertainty: A New Era of Measurement through Large Language Models
AB  - We measure uncertainty with large language models (LLMs), classifying 1.2 million Wall Street Journal articles from 1998 to mid-2025. The resulting indices cover economic policy, geopolitical risk, monetary policy, and financial market uncertainty. Validated against human-coded labels, they track human perception more closely than Bag-of-Words (BoW) benchmarks. They also capture articles that human readers judge to describe decreasing uncertainty, a category BoW methods cannot represent. For economic activity and flight-to-safety mutual fund flows, the indices carry explanatory power beyond existing measures. In an asset pricing application, they identify the source of volatility news.
