TI  - Writing homogenization post-ChatGPT: Corpus evidence from a decade-long study
AB  - Description: This repository contains supplementary computational materials for the manuscript Generative AI and the Emergence of Hybrid Authorship in academic writing: A Corpus-Based Analysis (2015–2024) published in the Modern Language Journal. The files provide complete R scripts for machine learning classification and statistical evaluation. The code operationalizes multidimensional feature extraction across learner corpora. It establishes a robust and reproducible methodological framework. Researchers can adopt this computational architecture using independent historical archives. This application establishes a known baseline of unaided human authorship. Consequently, educators can objectively quantify the impact of algorithmic text generation. The provided algorithms isolate the specific linguistic footprint of hybrid authorship. This repository ensures full computational reproducibility for the broader academic community.
